// It is now a working month calendar over the host's real availability.
//
// ── THE RULE THAT MATTERS: A NIGHT IS NOT A DAY ──────────────────────────
//
// listBlockedNights returns the nights already taken. A guest checking out on
// the 14th does NOT occupy the night of the 14th, so the next guest may check
// in that morning. The range validity check therefore covers checkIn up to but
// NOT INCLUDING checkOut.
//
// Getting this wrong in either direction is expensive: too strict and the
// calendar refuses back-to-back bookings that are perfectly legal, losing the
// host a night; too loose and two guests are sold the same night and someone
// arrives to a locked door. The server checks this again inside a transaction
// when the booking is created — this screen is the courtesy, not the
// guarantee.
//
// ── WHY THE TOTAL HERE IS AN ESTIMATE ────────────────────────────────────
//
// The bottom bar multiplies the listing's nightly rate by the number of
// nights. That is NOT the price. The service fee, any cashback and the deposit
// hold are decided by getStayQuote on the server, which is called on the next
// screen. This bar therefore says "before fees" rather than "Total", because a
// number that changes when you tap Continue is worse than no number at all.
